\pard\sb200\sa120\cf1\b 4. Activation, hardware binding and seats\b0\par
\pard\sa120\cf1 4.1 The Software requires activation with a licence token issued to your Easy OKAPI account. Accounts are created at https://www.easysensorkit.cbbiotec.vn/account/signup.\par
\pard\sa120\cf1 4.2 On activation the Software computes a hardware fingerprint of the machine \u8212? a SHA-256 digest of a stable operating-system machine identifier combined with a fixed salt \u8212? and the token is cryptographically bound to that fingerprint.\par
\pard\sa120\cf1 4.3 A token is valid on one machine. Copying an activated installation, or the activation.json file inside it, to a second machine will not work: the fingerprint will not match and the Software will refuse to start.\par
\pard\sa120\cf1 4.4 The Software contacts the Services at start-up and periodically thereafter to confirm the licence is still valid. When the machine is offline, the Software continues to run on its last known good state until the next successful check.\par
\pard\sa120\cf1 4.5 If you replace or reinstall a machine and need the seat moved, email tqmthong@gmail.com; we will revoke the old seat and issue a replacement.\par
\pard\sa120\cf1 4.6 Attempting to defeat, patch out, spoof or otherwise circumvent activation, the hardware binding, the seat limit or the revocation check is a material breach of this agreement, regardless of any right the MIT License gives you to modify the source code. The breach lies in your use of our Services, not in your editing of the code.\par
